sent a  masterpiece in a state in which we can  no longer see it today like the  engraving by morgan of leonardo's last  supper before its deterioration  it must be said that the results of this  interpretation of the art of gift giving  were not always brilliant  the idea formed a venice from a drawing  by titan that is supposed to have a  lagoon in the background was certainly  far less accurate than the one i would  have derived from simple photographs  we could not keep count at home and my  great aunt wanted to drop an indictment  against my grandmother the armchair she  presented young couples engaged to be  married or old married couples which is  the first attempt to make use of them  had immediately collapsed under the  weight of one of the recipients  but my grandmother would have believed  that petty to be overly concerned about  the solidity of a piece of wood which  one could still distinguish a small  flower a smile sometimes a lovely  invention from the past  even what might in these pieces of  furniture answer a need since it did so  in a matter to which we're no longer  accustomed gender like the old ways of  speaking in which we see a metaphor that  is obliterated in our modern language by  the aberration of habit  now in fact the pastoral novels of  george sand that she was giving me for  my saints day were like an old piece of  furniture full of expressions that had  fallen into disuse and turned figurative  again  the sword no longer find anywhere but in  the country  and my grandmother had bought them in  preference to others just as she would  sooner have rented an estate on which  there was a gothic dove code or another  those old things that exercise such a  happy influence in the mind by filling  it with longing for impossible voyages  through time  mama sat down by my bed  she had picked up josue whose reddish  cover an incomprehensible title gave it  to my eyes a distinct personality and a  mysterious attraction i not yet read a  real novel  i had heard people say that george sam  was an exemplary novelist this already  predisposed me to imagine something  indefinable indefinable and delicious in  france  narrative devices intended to arouse  curiosity or emotion  certain modes of expression that make  one uneasy or melancholy that a reader  with some education will recognize as  common in many novels appeared to me who  considered a new book not a thing not as  a thing having many counterparts but as  a unique person having no reason for  existing but in itself simply is a  disturbing emanation of frost water  shelby's peculiar essence  behind those events so ordinary those  things so common those words so currents  i sensed a strange sort of intonation  accentuation  the action began it seemed to me all the  more obscure because in those days when  i read i often daydream for entire pages  of something quite different  and in addition to the lacunae that this  distraction left in the story there was  the fact when mama was the one reading  aloud to me that she skipped all the  love scenes  there's all the bizarre changes that  take place in the respective attitudes  of the miller's wife and the child that  can be explained only by the progress of  a nascent love seem to me marked by  profound mystery whose source directly  imagined must be in that strange and  sweet name champio which gave the child  who wore without my knowing why it's  vivid charming purplish color  my mother was an unfaithful reader she  was also in the case of books in which  she found the inflection of true failing  a wonderful reader  for the respect and simplicity of her  interpretation the beauty and gentleness  of the sound of her voice  even in real life when it was people and  all works of art which moved into  compassion or admiration it was touching  to see with what deference she removed  from her voice from her emotions from  her words any spark of gaiety that might  hurt some mother who had once lost a  child  any 